WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.653
Today is six letters. Each one goes down, then bounces back up the same line, and over.

2
00:00:06.103 --> 00:00:12.915
Watch first. The first one on the page is done for you: show it, do the next one together, and your child does the rest.

3
00:00:13.415 --> 00:00:14.520
These six letters.

4
00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:17.699
Watch first. Then do the same with your child.

5
00:00:18.199 --> 00:00:23.583
Start at the dotted line. Pull down. Go back up the same line. Then over, just a little.

6
00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:28.919
This one starts the same. Down, up, over, and down again.

7
00:00:30.605 --> 00:00:35.058
And this one does it twice. Down, up, over, down. Up, over, down.

8
00:00:36.792 --> 00:00:40.583
The pencil does not lift. It goes back up the line it came down.

9
00:00:41.183 --> 00:00:46.114
This one is tall. Start at the top line. Pull down. Then up, over, and down.

10
00:00:47.509 --> 00:00:51.813
This one is tall too. Pull down from the top line. Then up, and around.

11
00:00:53.096 --> 00:00:59.349
This one has a tail. Start at the dotted line. Pull down below the bottom line. Then up, and around.

12
00:01:00.611 --> 00:01:03.022
Three kinds of letters live on the three lines.

13
00:01:03.472 --> 00:01:10.317
Tall letters reach the top line. Small letters stay under the dotted line. Tail letters hang below the bottom line.

14
00:01:10.767 --> 00:01:14.779
So for each big letter on the page, ask: tall, small, or tail?

15
00:01:15.229 --> 00:01:19.358
Your child finger-traces all six and says each path. Then step away.

16
00:01:19.808 --> 00:01:23.657
At the end, they write two letters and one word while you watch the pencil.
